questions.modelAnswer:
operation MarkState(qubits : Qubit[]) : Unit is Adj + Ctl {
    Controlled Z(qubits[0..Length(qubits)-2], qubits[Length(qubits)-1]);
}

operation Diffuser(qubits : Qubit[]) : Unit is Adj + Ctl {
    within {
        ApplyToEachA(H, qubits);
        ApplyToEachA(X, qubits);
    } apply {
        Controlled Z(qubits[0..Length(qubits)-2], qubits[Length(qubits)-1]);
    }
}

Declaring an operation 'is Adj + Ctl' tells the Q# compiler to automatically generate its adjoint (inverse) and controlled versions from the single forward definition, rather than requiring a separately hand-written inverse circuit. The within/apply block specifically runs the 'within' block, then the 'apply' block, then automatically the adjoint of the 'within' block — which is exactly the H...X...CZ...X...H diffuser pattern, but expressed without manually re-listing the closing H and X gates, because the compiler derives them as the adjoint of the opening ones. This is more compact and less error-prone than Qiskit's manual circuit style, where every gate in the 'undo' half has to be written out explicitly and kept in sync by hand if the circuit changes.

